==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|slug|-ish|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈslʌɡɪʃ/|[ˈslʌɡɪʃ]}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-sluggish.wav|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌɡɪʃ|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|slugg|ish}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er,more}}

# Habitually [[idle]] and [[lazy]]; [[slothful]]; [[dull]]; [[inactive]]
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:lazy}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''sluggish''' man}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Pharmacopolæ Justificati: Or, Apothecaries Vindicated from the Imputation of Ignorance.{{nb...|Wherein is Shown, that an Academical Education is No Way Necessary to Qualify a Man for the Practice of Physick.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed for}} J. Roberts,{{nb...|near the Oxford-Arms in Warwick-Lane.}}|year=1724|page=6|pageurl=https://books.google.com.sg/books?id=wgBcAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA6|oclc=990820804|passage=[I]f he leaves the School poſſeſs'd of a '''ſluggiſh''' indolent Diſpoſition, and of Learning rather forc'd upon him than choſen, it is probable he will forget what he brought thence; but if he be active, emulous and aſpiring, he will certainly find Time for Reading and Thinking; for tho' it be a homely, it is a true Saying, ''that where there is a Will, there is a Way''.}}
#* {{RQ:Rihani Khalid|chapter=On the Wharf of Enchantment|page=34|passage=He helps us to understand the insignificant points which mark the rapid undercurrents of the seemingly '''sluggish''' soul of Khalid.}}
# [[slow|Slow]]; having little [[motion]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:slow}}
#: {{ant|en|nimble}}
#* {{RQ:Jonson Coronation Triumph|sig=B3|verso=1|page=20|passage=Vp thou tame {{smallcaps|River}}, vvake; / And from the liquid limbes this ſlumber ſhake: / Thou drovvn'st thy ſelfe in inofficious ſleepe; / And theſe thy '''ſluggiſh''' vvaters ſeeme to creepe, / Rather than flovv.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=Robert M. Solow|title=Growth Theory: An Exposition|publisher=Oxford University Press|page=3
|passage=[T]he stock of capital is necessarily a '''sluggish''' time series, while output is capable of making wide swings in short intervals[.]}}
# Having no power to move oneself or itself; [[inert]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1695|author={{w|John Woodward (naturalist)|John Woodward}}|title=An Essay toward a Natural History of the Earth and Terrestrial Bodies
|passage=Matter, being impotent, '''sluggish''', and inactive, hath no power to stir or move itself.}}
# Characteristic of a [[sluggard]]; dull; [[stupid]]; [[tame]]; [[simple]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:stupid}}
# Exhibiting [[economic]] [[decline]], [[inactivity]], [[slow]], or [[subnormal]] [[growth]].
#: {{ux|en|Inflation has been rising despite a '''sluggish''' economy.}}
#: {{ux|en|Business is usually '''slow''' during the summer months.}}

